WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.115
Mastery Starter 11.0.

00:00:03.115 --> 00:00:05.570
New to Hedging & Risk Engineering?

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:06.630
Start here.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.717
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:10.410
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.165
Risk you don't want can often be hedged,

00:00:14.165 --> 00:00:16.740
insured or engineered away, at a cost.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.540
This module covers hedging, cover, liquidation protection,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.666
stress testing and what to do in

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:24.405
the first hour of a crisis.

00:00:25.705 --> 00:00:28.680
Hedge: a position that offsets another's risk.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.649
Protective put: an option capping downside below a price.

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:35.659
Cover: on-chain insurance for defined events.

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:38.184
Stress test: a what-if shock on your book.

00:00:38.184 --> 00:00:40.958
Incident: an exploit, depeg or compromise.

00:00:42.258 --> 00:00:43.843
Modules 0–10.

00:00:45.143 --> 00:00:47.211
Write down the single event that would

00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:49.386
hurt your portfolio most, and what you'd

00:00:49.386 --> 00:00:50.818
do in the first 10 minutes.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:55.117
Beginner: Knows the hedge tools and what they cost.

00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:57.935
Practitioner: Hedges one real exposure and

00:00:57.935 --> 00:01:00.004
runs the five stress tests.

00:01:00.004 --> 00:01:01.948
Master: Runs a stress-tested book

00:01:01.948 --> 00:01:03.949
with a rehearsed incident playbook.

00:01:05.249 --> 00:01:07.820
You've mastered this module when your book

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.451
survives all five stress scenarios and your

00:01:10.451 --> 00:01:12.544
incident playbook is saved offline.

00:01:13.844 --> 00:01:16.359
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:16.359 --> 00:01:19.137
Next up, Lesson 11.1: Hedging price

00:01:19.137 --> 00:01:21.607
exposure with perps and options.
